  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ID - Children and Families Together CAFT - I</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Bureau for Inclusive Growth, Partnerships, and Innovation (IPI)):  The CAFT-I Consortium will collaborate with the Indian government to significantly change and improve the childcare reform system, working within the current formal and informal schemes and structures, to ensure that all children grow up in families. To achieve this, the consortium will develop care reform strategies in up to 11 states, while building evidence that community-based  protection results in prevention of family separation in one state (Jharkhand). The project ensures that children with disabilities are prioritized. The KHSI-led Consortium brings extensive experience in care reform, disability rights and  inclusion, community and family strengthening and supporting governments. This activity advances implementation of the U.S. government Thrive Strategy.</narrative>
  </description>
